# The indent and marker fold methods, and switching between methods.

=== foldmethod indent closes every fold at foldlevel 0
ref:    fold.txt *fold-indent*
quote:  The folds are automatically defined by the indent of the lines.
given:
  |a
    b
      c
    d
  e
keys:   :set fdm=indent sw=2<CR>jj
expect:
  a
    b
      c
    d
  |e

=== foldmethod indent nests deeper indents
ref:    fold.txt *fold-indent*
quote:  A sequence of lines with the same or higher fold level form a fold, with the lines with a higher level forming a nested fold.
given:
  |a
    b
      c
      d
    e
  f
keys:   :set fdm=indent sw=2<CR>jzojj
expect:
  a
    b
      c
      d
  |  e
  f

=== foldmethod indent uses shiftwidth
ref:    fold.txt *fold-indent*
quote:  The foldlevel is computed from the indent of the line, divided by the 'shiftwidth' (rounded down).
given:
  |a
    b
      c
    d
  e
keys:   :set fdm=indent sw=4<CR>jzojj
expect:
  a
    b
      c
  |  d
  e

=== zR opens every indent fold
ref:    fold.txt *zR*
quote:  Open all folds.
given:
  |a
    b
      c
    d
keys:   :set fdm=indent sw=2<CR>zRjj
expect:
  a
    b
  |    c
    d

=== foldlevel 1 leaves indent folds of level 1 open
ref:    options.txt *'foldlevel'*
quote:  Sets the fold level: Folds with a higher level will be closed.
given:
  |a
    b
      c
      d
    e
  f
keys:   :set fdm=indent sw=2 fdl=1<CR>jjjj
expect:
  a
    b
      c
      d
    e
  |f

=== empty lines take the lower fold level around them
ref:    fold.txt *fold-indent*
quote:  Some lines are ignored and get the fold level of the line above or below it, whichever is lower.
given:
  |a
    b
  
    c
  d
keys:   :set fdm=indent sw=2<CR>jj
expect:
  a
    b
  
    c
  |d

=== an empty line between indent levels ends the fold
ref:    fold.txt *fold-indent*
quote:  These are empty or white lines and lines starting with a character in 'foldignore'.
given:
  |a
    b
  
  c
keys:   :set fdm=indent sw=2<CR>jj
expect:
  a
    b
  |
  c

=== dd on an indent fold deletes the block
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When using an operator, a closed fold is included as a whole.
given:
  a
  |  b
      c
  d
keys:   :set fdm=indent sw=2<CR>dd
expect:
  a
  |d

=== numbered markers start folds of that level
ref:    fold.txt *{{{*
quote:  A fold starts at a "{{{" marker. The following number specifies the fold level.
given:
  |a {{{1
  b
  c {{{1
  d
  e
keys:   :set fdm=marker<CR>j
expect:
  a {{{1
  b
  |c {{{1
  d
  e

=== a higher numbered marker starts a nested fold
ref:    fold.txt *{{{*
quote:  If a marker with a higher fold level is found, a nested fold is started.
given:
  |a {{{1
  b
  c {{{2
  d
  e {{{1
  f
keys:   :set fdm=marker<CR>zojjj
expect:
  a {{{1
  b
  c {{{2
  d
  |e {{{1
  f

=== a lower numbered marker ends the nested folds
ref:    fold.txt *{{{*
quote:  If a marker with a lower fold level is found, all folds up to and including this level end and a fold with the specified level starts.
given:
  |a {{{1
  b {{{2
  c {{{3
  d
  e {{{1
  f
keys:   :set fdm=marker<CR>j
expect:
  a {{{1
  b {{{2
  c {{{3
  d
  |e {{{1
  f

=== matching marker pairs nest
ref:    fold.txt *{{{*
quote:  Each "{{{" increases the fold level by one, each "}}}" decreases the fold level by one.
given:
  |a {{{
  b
  c {{{
  d
  }}}
  e }}}
  f
keys:   :set fdm=marker<CR>zojjj
expect:
  a {{{
  b
  c {{{
  d
  }}}
  |e }}}
  f

=== a closed marker fold covers both markers
ref:    fold.txt *{{{*
quote:  Each "{{{" increases the fold level by one, each "}}}" decreases the fold level by one.
given:
  |a {{{
  b
  }}}
  c
keys:   :set fdm=marker<CR>j
expect:
  a {{{
  b
  }}}
  |c

=== a numbered end marker ends the fold of that level
ref:    fold.txt *{{{*
quote:  You can use "}}}" with a digit to indicate the level of the fold that ends.
given:
  |a {{{1
  b {{{2
  c }}}2
  d
  e
keys:   :set fdm=marker<CR>zojjj
expect:
  a {{{1
  b {{{2
  c }}}2
  d
  |e

=== a marker with level zero is ignored
ref:    fold.txt *{{{*
quote:  A zero cannot be used (a marker with level zero is ignored).
given:
  |a {{{0
  b
  c
keys:   :set fdm=marker<CR>j
expect:
  a {{{0
  |b
  c

=== zj moves to the next marker fold
ref:    fold.txt *zj*
quote:  Move downwards to the start of the next fold.
given:
  |a
  b {{{
  c }}}
  d
keys:   :set fdm=marker<CR>zj
expect:
  a
  |b {{{
  c }}}
  d

=== setting foldmethod indent replaces manual folds
ref:    fold.txt *fold-methods*
quote:  When setting 'foldmethod' to a value other than "manual", all folds are deleted and new ones created.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   zfj:set fdm=indent<CR>j
expect:
  one
  |two
  three

=== switching to manual keeps the folds
ref:    fold.txt *fold-methods*
quote:  Switching to the "manual" method doesn't remove the existing folds.
given:
  |a
    b
    c
  d
keys:   :set fdm=indent sw=2<CR>:set fdm=manual<CR>jj
expect:
  a
    b
    c
  |d

=== zd on a fold kept from indent deletes it
ref:    fold.txt *fold-methods*
quote:  This can be used to first define the folds automatically and then change them manually.
given:
  |a
    b
    c
  d
keys:   :set fdm=indent sw=2<CR>:set fdm=manual<CR>jzdj
expect:
  a
    b
  |  c
  d
